# Response headers for stashfm.app. Cloudflare Workers Static Assets reads this
# file at deploy time and doesn't serve it. (`npm run preview` ignores it; use
# `npx wrangler dev` to see these headers locally.)
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the site's privacy promise, enforced by the
# browser: fonts, images and styles may only come from stashfm.app itself, and no
# script runs at all. Cloudflare leaves this header alone, except that Zaraz
# rewrites it so its own script can run: one more reason Zaraz stays off
# (web/README.md, "Privacy rules for the site itself").
# It covers only the files Cloudflare serves without running the Worker (see
# run_worker_first in wrangler.jsonc). Everything the Worker answers, the home page
# and the early-access pages included, gets the same headers from worker/pages.js
# (SECURITY_HEADERS); keep the two in step (a test checks the CSP matches).
# form-action 'self': the sign-in and request forms post to this site only.
# The share Worker's pages on the same domain (/t, /m, /l) send their own headers
# from infra/share-worker.
# If something you add doesn't load in production, this is why. Self-host it instead.
# - The pages need inline styles (Astro inlines small stylesheets, the font rules
#   and a few style attributes) and data: images (small SVG icons inside the CSS).
# - If the site ever needs a script, allow that one script by its sha256 hash in
#   script-src, not with 'unsafe-inline' or 'self', which would also allow the
#   inline and /cdn-cgi/ scripts that some Cloudflare features add to pages.
#
# Caching: there is no long Cache-Control rule for /_astro/*, on purpose. These
# rules match the request path whatever the status, so a missing /_astro/ file
# would get the 404 page with a one-year cache, and a browser would keep that 404
# even after the file exists again (after a rollback, for example). Without a
# rule, every file gets Cloudflare's default, `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# with an ETag: a returning browser checks each file and gets a short
# 304 Not Modified when it hasn't changed. Don't add a long cache back unless a
# Worker removes it from responses that aren't 200.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'none'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
